                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5331/136: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-31T15:00:00+01:00">March 31, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 31—1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Department’s telegram March 30, 6 p.m. In other cases, notably Germany and
                    Japan, Portugal has conceded abolition of flag discrimination on a temporary
                    basis, pending negotiations. I believe that firm insistence on such a minimum
                    would add to American prestige here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
